{"title":"1998 AJHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three generous friends, each with some cash, redistribute the money as follows:\nAmi gives enough money to Jan and Toy to double the amount that each has.\nJan then gives enough to Ami and Toy to double their amounts. \nFinally, Toy gives Ami and Jan enough to double their amounts.\nIf Toy has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da293ec0bca4ae0f7aa972734e72a090692d331d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> when they begin and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da293ec0bca4ae0f7aa972734e72a090692d331d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> when they end, what is the total amount that all three friends have?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/a/8fae15d7007536e7125d85e46b8495a4151ddd16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\$108\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\$180\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\$216\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\$252\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\$288$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"487\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After Ami gives money to Toy and Jan, Toy has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/2/2a226c85e6ed60c592e54d5f142103781d72ca6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\$36 = \\$72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>After Jan gives money to Ami and Toy, Toy has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07fd2727bbcc82e6dce73c675d734c152d5235fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\$72 = \\$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, Toy gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bbaa6cdf8e7faf119b409f6a908373a06e8a4b79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$144 - \\$36 = \\$108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"17\" /> to Jan and Ami.  Since Jan and Ami each doubled their money, they must have had a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b5131c648a0f8bba53472604ae71a1cc07ea01c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" /> before Toy gave them money and thus now have a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e60423cf00bff597a01749f4d747c307d95d6c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\$108 = \\$216$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" />.  \n</p><p>Therefore, the three friends have a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2ca955738d8bbe077f45dabe4274be2017b7618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$216 + \\$36 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\$252}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"195\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align: